      "body": "_Posted by Kunal's robot (Claude Opus 5.5) ↓_\n>\n> ## Motivation\n>\n> `determine_tensor_transport_mode()` falls back to inline (pickled) feature transport whenever `nnodes > 1`. With pipeline parallelism, only the first stage's TP group reads tokenizer output, so shared memory still works when that group sits on node 0 with the tokenizer:\n>\n> ```\n> node 0                            node 1..n\n> tokenizer --shm--> PP0 TP group   PP1..PPn (requests relayed by PP0)\n> ```\n>\n> Launchers that start one process group per GPU report even a single-host PP engine as `nnodes == pp_size`. In that setup the tokenizer manager pickles every request's decoded pixel tensors (hundreds of MB for several large images) on its event loop, which stalls all other requests and `/health`.\n>\n> ## Modifications\n>\n> - Keep shared-memory transport when `nnodes > 1` if each TP group fits on one node (`nnodes <= pp_size`), there are no data-parallel replicas (`dp_size == 1`), and the launch does not use Ray, whose placement groups can put any rank on any node.\n> - Extend `test_tensor_transport_mode.py` with the PP, DP and Ray cases.\n>\n> The first stage still pickles materialized features when it relays requests to the next stage. That is unchanged by this PR and could be a follow-up.\n>\n> This PR is independent of #44575 and #44576, which address the same workload.\n>\n> ## Accuracy Tests\n>\n> Not applicable: the change only picks the transport for feature tensors.\n>\n> ## Speed Tests and Profiling\n>\n> A PP8 prefill server under image traffic for 30 minutes: 0.2 requests per second, 4 images per request, 59k to 74k prompt tokens. Base is `main`; fixed has this PR and #44575 and #44576.\n>\n> | Metric | Base | Fixed |\n> |---|---|---|\n> | `/v1/models` p90 | 70 ms | under 5 ms |\n> | `/v1/models` p99 | 550 ms | under 5 ms |\n> | `/v1/models` max | 1.08 s | 10 ms |\n> | `/health` probes over 5 s | 143 | 14 |\n> | Request p50 | 15.3 s | 13.1 s |\n>\n> ## Checklist\n>\n> - [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n> - [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n> - [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not needed.\n> - [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n> - [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38806970576](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38806970576)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38806970410](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38806970410)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38806970432](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38806970432)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
